# B) Backend — Convex Architecture

This is where real changes happen.

---

## B1. Core Architecture

Backend: Convex (TypeScript)

Components:

* Queries (read)
* Mutations (write)
* Actions (external calls, storage, AI)
* Scheduled functions (cron)
* HTTP actions (for PDF export if needed)

No separate Fastify API layer in baseline Plan B.

Optional:
Retain thin external server only for:

* Advanced AI proxy control
* Complex report generation
* Regulatory isolation

But default architecture:
Mobile → Convex directly

---

## B2. Data Layer

Database: Convex document database

Collections:

* users
* logs
* routines
* routineCompletions
* insights
* chatMessages
* weeklyReports

Design constraint:

* One user_id on every document
* Explicit per-user access checks inside every query/mutation

There is no RLS like Postgres.
Security enforced via Convex auth + explicit checks in code.

Invariant:
Every query must filter by authenticated user ID.

---

## B3. Authentication

Auth provider options:

Option A (simplest):

* Convex Auth + Apple Sign-In
* Email/password fallback

Option B (more control):

* Clerk or Auth0 integrated with Convex

All Convex functions:

* Use authenticated identity context
* Reject unauthenticated access immediately

---

## B4. Storage (PHI Photos)

Convex file storage OR external provider (recommended):

Recommended:

* Cloudflare R2
* Google Cloud Storage
* AWS S3

Flow:

1. Client requests upload token via Convex action
2. Signed URL returned
3. Client uploads directly
4. File reference stored in Convex

Invariant:

* No raw photos stored in logs document
* Only storage reference ID

---

## B5. Logging & Routine Mutations

Convex Mutations:

* createLog
* updateLog
* toggleRoutineCompletion
* createRoutine
* updateRoutine
* deleteRoutine
* syncDraftLog

Convex Queries:

* getTodayLog
* getWeeklyLogs
* getRoutineStatus
* getInsights
* getChatHistory

All writes validated via zod.

---

## B6. AI / Insights Architecture (Convex Version)

Two-Layer Insight Model retained.

### Instant Insights (Non-LLM)

* Executed in mutation after log save
* Deterministic rules
* Stored in insights collection
* Fully explainable

Zero external calls.

---

### Reflective Insights (LLM)

Executed via Convex Action.

Flow:

1. Query aggregated logs
2. Pass through PHI Transform layer
3. Send anonymized aggregate to LLM
4. Store response with confidence metadata

Guardrails:

* No raw free-text notes
* No image data
* Conservative language enforcement

---

## B7. PHI Transform Library (Convex Variant)

Still mandatory.

Transformations:

* Strip free text
* Aggregate counts
* Bucket time ranges
* Remove exact timestamps
* No user identifiers

Invariant:
LLM never sees identifiable PHI.

---

## B8. Background Jobs

Convex scheduled functions:

* Weekly insight generation
* Routine adherence aggregation
* Cleanup expired drafts
* Trigger risk recalculation

Monitoring:

* Execution latency
* Error frequency
* External API cost

---

## B9. Security & Compliance Adjustments

Because Convex lacks RLS:

Security model shifts to:

* Auth-based user isolation
* Explicit user_id checks in every function
* No admin bypass functions exposed
* Audit log collection for sensitive reads

Service keys:

* Never in client
* Only in Convex environment variables

